\mt1 Malaki
\mt2 (Malachi)
\is1 Introduction
\ip This document records some of God's messages that were given to the prophet Malaki (more accurately ‘Malʼākī’, although traditionally spelt as ‘Malachi’) to pass on to the Israeli people. It was written around 500 years before Yeshua/Jesus (B.C.) once the replacement temple was finished in Yerushalem (Jerusalem). The main purpose of the messages is to encourage the priests and the people to turn back to God and obey him from their hearts. It's apparent that many of them were no longer obeying and worshipping God. The priests and the people were short-changing God by offering second-class animals for the sacrifices and none of them were following God's desires. But God intervened in order to judge and restore his people, and he will send a teacher to precede him to prepare the path and to restore his agreement.
\iot Main components of this account
\io1 The sins of the Israelis \ior 1:1–2:16\ior*
\io1 God's judgement and mercy \ior 2:17–4:6\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\p
\v 1 This is a message¦380162 that Yahweh¦380164 gave to¦380165 Malaki¦380169 for the¦380168 Israelis¦380167:
\s1 Yahweh's love for the Israelis
\rem /s1 The Lord's Love for Israel; Jacob Loved, Esau Hated; Religious decline and hope of recovery; Israel Preferred to Edom; The Lord's Love for Israel
\p
\v 2 “I¦380186 have loved¦380171 you all,” says¦380173 Yahweh¦380174, \add ≈but¦380175\add* you say¦380175, “How¦380176 have you \add shown your\add* love for us¦380177?”
\p “Wasn't Esaw¦380181 Yacob's¦380182 brother¦380180?” declares Yahweh. “Yet I've¦380171 loved Yacob\x + \xo 1:2-3: \xt Rom 9:13.\x*
\v 3 and \add ≈rejected\add* Esaw. I've¦380195 turned¦380195 the hills¦380198 \add where Esaw lived\add* into a wasteland¦380199 and \add given\add* his¦380202 inheritance¦380202 to the wild jackals¦380203.”
\p
\v 4 If \add Esaw's descendants in\add* Edom¦380209 say, “We've \add ≈been¦380210 crushed\add*, but we'll¦380211 return¦380211 and \add ≈rebuild¦380212 what was¦380229 destroyed\add*,” then army-commander¦380217 Yahweh will say, “They¦380218 might build¦380219, but I¦380220 will tear¦380221 down¦380221. Others will call¦380222 them¦380223 ‘The country of¦380224 wickedness¦380225’ and ‘The people¦380226 who Yahweh is forever¦380233 angry with.’
\p
\v 5 Your¦380235 own¦380235 eyes¦380235 will¦380236 see¦380236 it, and¦380237 you'll say¦380238, ‘Yahweh¦380240 is¦380239 great¦380239 even outside Yisrael's¦380243 borders¦380242.’ ”
\s1 Second-class sacrifices
\rem /s1 The Lord Reprimands the Priests; Unworthy Sacrifices; Blemished Sacrifices; Corruption of the Priesthood
\p
\v 6 “A son¦380245 honours his father, and¦380248 a servant¦380248 \add ≡honours\add* his master, \add ≈so\add* if¦380250 I'm a father, where is my honour¦380255? If¦380256 I am¦380258 a master, where is my respect¦380261?” says¦380262 army-commander¦380265 Yahweh¦380264 to¦380266 all you priests¦380267 who¦380268 despise¦380268 my name¦380275.
\p “But¦380248 you say¦380270, ‘How¦380271 have¦380272 we¦380272 despised¦380272 your¦380275 name?’
\v 7 By offering polluted food¦380281 on¦380284 my¦380280 altar¦380280. But¦380283 you say¦380283, ‘How¦380284 have¦380285 we¦380285 polluted you?’ By saying¦380286 that Yahweh's¦380288 table¦380287 can \add just\add* be disrespected.
\v 8 Don't¦380297 you think it's¦380305 wrong¦380298 when you sacrifice¦380296 blind¦380295 animals? Isn't it evil¦380298 when you offer¦380294 lame¦380301 or sick¦380302 \add ≡animals\add*? Try presenting¦380305 them to¦380307 your¦380314 governor¦380307! Will¦380308 he welcome you or would¦380313 he \add ≈be¦380308 offended\add*?” says¦380315 army-commander¦380317 Yahweh¦380316.\x + \xo 1:8: \xt Deu 15:21.\x*
\p
\v 9 \add ≈So¦380319 now¦380319\add* bring you requests to God¦380325 and¦380319 \add ≈hope to be showered by his grace\add*. \add Ha,\add* army-commander¦380336 Yahweh¦380335 \add ≈asks how he¦380331 could¦380326 treat you all favourably¦380326 when you're bringing second-class offerings\add*?
\p
\v 10 “Yeah, if only there¦380349 was one \add >person\add* among¦380341 you who¦380338 would shut¦380342 the¦380343 temple gates so that you all couldn't \add just continue\add* to¦380346 light¦380346 worthless fires on¦380341 my¦380347 altar¦380347. I get no pleasure¦380352 from¦380361 you all,” says¦380354 army-commander¦380356 Yahweh¦380355, “and¦380342 I won't¦380344 accept¦380360 any offering¦380357 \add ≈that you all bring me¦380351\add*.
\v 11 People in other countries from¦380364 the east \add all the way\add* to the west will honour me, and incense¦380376 and genuine sacrifices will be offered¦380379 to me, because¦380381 my¦380378 reputation¦380371 in those countries will be praised,” says¦380386 army-commander¦380388 Yahweh¦380387.
\v 12 “But¦380392 you all are¦380391 dishonouring \add @my¦380395 name\add* when you say¦380393 that the¦380394 master's¦380395 table¦380394 is¦380396 polluted, and¦380390 that its fruit¦380398, its food¦380400, can be treated with¦380393 contempt.
\v 13 You all also¦380405 say¦380402, ‘How tiresome this is,’ and¦380402 you snort at¦380405 it¦380406,” says army-commander¦380409 Yahweh. “You all bring¦380410 \add animals\add* for your offering¦380421 that were killed by a wild animal or is lame¦380414 or sick¦380417. Should I¦380422 accept¦380422 those from¦380424 you?” says Yahweh.
\v 14 “May the cheats be cursed¦380429 who¦380430 have male¦380433 animals in¦380432 their flocks¦380432 and vow¦380434 to give them, but¦380429 instead sacrifices¦380435 a second-class animal to the master¦380437! Yes, I'm a powerful king¦380439,” says¦380442 army-commander¦380444 Yahweh¦380443, “and my¦380445 name¦380445 will be carefully respected among¦380447 the nations¦380447.”
\c 2
\s1 A warning for the priests
\rem /s1 Admonition for the Priests; A Warning for the Priests
\p
\v 1 Now¦380453 you priests¦380453, this¦380452 command¦380451 is¦380450 for all of you:
\v 2 Army-commander¦380471 Yahweh¦380470 says¦380469, “If¦380459 you all won't listen¦380458 and¦380459 won't \add ≈decide in your minds\add* to honour¦380467 to my \add ≈reputation¦380468\add*, then I'll send¦380472 a curse on¦380473 you all—\add ≈in fact\add* I'll curse your blessings¦380480. Indeed, I've¦380482 \add already\add* cursed¦380482 them, because¦380483 you all are¦380485 not¦380457 \add ≈internalising\add* \add <my instructions\add*.
\v 3 Listen, I'm¦380490 about¦380491 to¦380491 rebuke¦380491 your descendants, and I'll¦380496 spread¦380496 the¦380501 offal from your festivals¦380502 on¦380498 your faces¦380500, and you all will¦380503 be taken¦380503 away¦380503 with it¦380505.
\v 4 That's¦380508 so you'll all know¦380507 that it's me who sent¦380509 this¦380513 command¦380512 to¦380514 you: so that my¦380515 agreement¦380515 with¦380516 the¦380512 Levites can continue,” says¦380519 army-commander¦380521 Yahweh¦380520.\x + \xo 2:4: \xt Num 3:11-13.\x*
\p
\v 5 “My¦380523 agreement with¦380526 \add @your¦380523 ancestor Levi\add* was \add to give\add* life¦380527 and peace¦380528, and I¦380529 gave¦380529 them to \add #them\add*. It¦380531 was an agreement \add ≈based on respect\add*, and \add #they\add* respected me¦380533 and \add ≈honoured\add* my¦380535 name¦380535.\x + \xo 2:5: \xt Num 25:12.\x*
\v 6 \add ≈They taught the people what was¦380541 right¦380540 and true—they didn't¦380544 tell lies\add*. \add #They\add* \add ≈worked for me¦380551 peacefully¦380548 and loyally\add*, and they \add ≈encouraged many¦380552 people to stop disobeying\add*.
\v 7 \add ≈Yes,\add* priests¦380559 should pass on knowledge¦380562 and¦380563 people¦380564 should look to \add #them\add* \add ≈for¦380556 good¦380556 teaching¦380556\add*, because¦380566 they¦380560 are army-commander¦380570 Yahweh's¦380568 messengers¦380567.
\p
\v 8 But¦380573 you all have turned¦380574 away from¦380575 \add that\add* path¦380577 and¦380573 have caused¦380578 many¦380579 \add >people\add* to¦380578 stumble¦380578 \add ≈because of¦380582 what you've taught\add*—you all have corrupted¦380581 the¦380582 agreement¦380582 with¦380580 Levi¦380583,” says¦380584 army-commander¦380586 Yahweh¦380585.
\v 9 “So¦380588 that's¦380599 why I've¦380591 caused you all to¦380595 be despised¦380593 by all the people¦380597 and¦380588 humiliated—because¦380598 you all haven't \add ≈followed me\add*, but¦380588 rather you've been biased in¦380607 matters¦380598 of¦380598 the law.”
\s1 The people have been unfaithful
\rem /s1 A Call to Faithfulness; The Covenant Profaned by Judah; Judah Unfaithful; The People's Unfaithfulness to God
\p
\v 10 Don't¦380610 we all have one father¦380611? Didn't the one God¦380615 create¦380617 us¦380617 all? \add So\add* why¦380618 do¦380619 we cheat each¦380620 other, thus disrespecting the agreement¦380623 with¦380621 our¦380613 ancestors¦380624?
\v 11 \add Our nation of\add* Yehudah¦380627 \add !(Judah¦380627)\add* has¦380626 been¦380629 unfaithful \add to Yahweh\add* and done¦380629 detestable things in Yisrael¦380630 and in Yerushalem¦380631. \add ≈Our men\add* have defiled the¦380636 temple that¦380638 Yahweh loves¦380639 by \add ≈marrying¦380640 foreign¦380644 women who worship pagan gods¦380643\add*.
\v 12 May¦380646 Yahweh, the one who is awake and¦380652 the one who answers¦380652, banish the \add #men\add* who do¦380650 this from¦380653 Yisrael, even if \add #they\add* are bringing¦380655 an¦380656 offering¦380656 to¦380657 army-commander¦380658 Yahweh.
\p
\v 13 Secondly¦380666, you cover¦380664 Yahweh's¦380669 altar¦380668 with tears from¦380672 all your weeping¦380670 and groaning¦380671 because¦380672 he still¦380673 ignores your offerings¦380677 and won't¦380672 accept¦380678 what you all bring to¦380675 him.
\v 14 \add ≈So¦380682\add* you \add ≈ask\add*, “Why not?” \add Well,\add* it's because¦380687 Yahweh¦380689 can testify¦380690 that you've¦380698 been unfaithful to the¦380694 wife¦380694 that you \add ≈married\add* when you were young, even though she¦380700 was¦380701 your companion¦380701, and¦380682 despite your vows.
\v 15 Didn't \add @Yahweh¦380708\add* make¦380708 \add you and your wife\add* one¦380707 and give you some of¦380709 his spirit because he¦380708 wanted godly children \add to come from your marriage\add*? \add ≈So¦380705\add* guard¦380717 yourselves in¦380718 your spirit, and don't¦380705 be unfaithful to the¦380719 \add ≈woman you married when you were young\add*.
\p
\v 16 “Indeed, I hate¦380727 divorce,” says Yahweh, the¦380731 god¦380731 of¦380731 Yisrael¦380732, “and \add ≈so-called ‘good people’ who are actually cruel\add*,” says army-commander¦380740 Yahweh. “So \add ≈listen to your consciences\add* and don't¦380743 be unfaithful.”
\s1 Judgement day is coming
\rem /s1 The Day of Judgment; The Day of Judgment Is Near
\p
\v 17 You've all wearied Yahweh with your¦380753 words¦380749, and \add yet\add* you \add ≈ask¦380750\add*, “How¦380751 have¦380747 we¦380752 wearied him¦380752?” By¦380753 saying¦380753, “Yahweh is pleased \add even\add* with those who¦380756 do evil¦380757, and he's¦380763 happy with \add all\add* of them¦380762,” or¦380765 “Where¦380766 is the¦380767 god¦380767 of justice¦380768?”
\c 3
\rem /s1 The Coming Day of Judgment; The Coming Messenger
\p
\v 1 “Listen, I'm¦380770 about to send¦380771 my¦380772 messenger and¦380773 he'll prepare¦380773 the path¦380775 ahead¦380776 of¦380772 me¦380776. Then the master¦380782 who you're all looking¦380787 for¦380787 will¦380778 suddenly¦380777 come to his¦380781 temple¦380781, \add yes,\add* the messenger who you are¦380793 all happy about—the party to the agreement¦380789—he'll come,” says¦380797 army-commander¦380799 Yahweh¦380798.\x + \xo 3:1: \xt Mat 11:10; Mrk 1:2; Luk 1:76; 7:27.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈But¦380801 who¦380801 could survive it when he comes¦380806\add*? Who¦380803 can stand¦380808 when he appears¦380809, because¦380810 he'll be like the refiner's¦380814 fire¦380813 and¦380801 like the cleaners' \add powerful\add* soap?\x + \xo 3:2: \xt Yoel 2:11; Rev 6:17.\x*
\v 3 \add @Yahweh¦380833\add* will act as a refiner¦380819 and purifier¦380820 of¦380825 silver, and he will purify¦380822 Levi's¦380827 descendants¦380825 \add the priests\add*—\add yes,\add* he'll¦380818 refine¦380828 \add &you all\add* \add with fire\add* like¦380830 gold¦380830 and silver, and \add &you'll\add* bring¦380834 offerings¦380835 to¦380833 \add *him¦380834\add* that are \add ≈acceptable\add*.
\v 4 \add After that,\add* the offerings¦380840 of \add the people of\add* Yudah¦380841 and Yerushalem¦380842 will¦380838 be¦380838 pleasing¦380838 to¦380839 Yahweh¦380839, as in \add ≈ancient times\add*, and as in previous years¦380845.
\p
\v 5 This is what army-commander¦380872 Yahweh¦380871 says¦380870, “At that time, I'll come to you all to judge¦380850 you. I'll quickly testify against all those who practice sorcery¦380855, \add ≡against\add* adulterers¦380856, \add ≡against\add* those who \add ≈lie in¦380855 court\add*, \add ≡against\add* those who \add ≈don't pay their workers fairly\add*, \add ≡against\add* those who mistreat widows¦380863 and orphans¦380864, \add ≡against\add* those who \add ≈don't treat the¦380860 foreigners among you decently\add*, and \add ≡against\add* those who \add ≈refuse to honour\add* me¦380869.
\s1 Giving a tenth
\rem /s1 The Payment of Tithes; Robbing God; A Call to Repentance
\p
\v 6 “I am Yahweh¦380876 and¦380879 I don't¦380877 change¦380878—that's the¦380880 \add only\add* reason why you descendants¦380880 of¦380880 Yacob¦380882 haven't been destroyed.
\v 7 Ever since¦380886 the¦380886 time¦380886 when your ancestors¦380887 were alive, you all have¦380888 \add ≈ignored my¦380889 commands\add* and¦380890 \add ≈refused to obey\add* them¦380891. \add Now\add* return to me—\add if you all do so,\add* I'll¦380894 return to you. That's what I, army-commander¦380898 Yahweh¦380897, say¦380899. But¦380890 you all ask, ‘How¦380900 can we¦380901 return to you?’
\rem /s1 Don't rob God
\v 8 Can a human rob¦380903 God¦380905? \add Yes,\add* you're all robbing me¦380909, but¦380910 you ask, ‘How¦380911 are¦380908 we¦380912 robbing you?’ \add By failing to give\add* a tenth plus¦380910 offerings¦380914.
\v 9 You're¦380919 all¦380923 cursed¦380916 because you're robbing¦380921 me—the whole¦380923 nation¦380922 of you.
\v 10 Bring¦380925 the full tenth into¦380931 the temple storeroom¦380934, so that there'll be¦380935 food¦380936 in¦380937 my¦380937 house¦380937 \add for the temple workers\add*,” says¦380941 army-commander¦380943 Yahweh¦380942. “\add In fact,\add* you all can test¦380938 me¦380938 \add ≈by¦380940 doing that and see\add* if¦380944 I¦380947 don't¦380946 open¦380947 the windows¦380950 of¦380950 heaven¦380951 for you all and pour¦380952 out¦380952 an \add ≈overflowing\add* blessing¦380954 for you.\x + \xo 3:10: \xt Lev 27:30; Num 18:21-24; Deu 12:6; 14:22-29; Neh 13:12.\x*
\v 11 I'll¦380968 rebuke¦380961 the devourer¦380963\f + \fr 3:11 \ft This is literally the ‘eater’ which could refer to some kind of insect (and hence ‘\+em it\+em* won't destroy’ in the next clause) or it could refer to some spiritual power (then you'd get ‘\+em he\+em* won't destroy’).\f* for¦380967 you all, so that it¦380974 won't destroy¦380966 your crops, and¦380961 the fruit¦380970 off your vines¦380976 in¦380977 the countryside¦380977 won't be lost,” says¦380978 army-commander¦380980 Yahweh¦380979.
\v 12 “Then¦380983 all the¦380986 other countries¦380986 would say that you've all been blessed¦380982, because¦380987 your¦380984 land¦380991 \add ≈would be¦380989 prosperous\add*,” says¦380993 army-commander¦380995 Yahweh¦380994.
\s1 God promises mercy for some
\rem /s1 The righteous triumphant; God's Promise of Mercy
\p
\v 13 “Your words¦381000 against me¦380999 have been¦380998 harsh,” says¦381001 Yahweh¦381002. “But¦381003 you all say¦381003, ‘What¦381004 have we¦381006 said among ourselves against you?’
\v 14 You've all said¦381009, ‘It's \add ≈a waste of time\add* serving¦381011 God¦381012. What¦381013 did we¦381017 gain by keeping¦381017 his¦381018 requirements¦381018, or by \add ≈being sorrowful\add* in¦381022 front¦381022 of army-commander¦381024 Yahweh¦381023?
\v 15 \add ≈It seems that¦381033 arrogant¦381029 people are¦381028 happier\add*. Evil people not only prosper, but¦381026 they¦381036 \add even\add* \add ≈challenge God¦381037 yet nothing happens to them\add*.’ ”
\rem /s1 The Reward of the Faithful; The Lord's Promise of Mercy
\p
\v 16 Then¦381040 those who \add ≈still respected\add* Yahweh spoke¦381041 with¦381045 one another. Yahweh paid¦381048 attention¦381048 and listened¦381050, and \add ≈while he¦381050 watched\add*, a book of¦381052 remembrance¦381053 was¦381051 written¦381051 about¦381042 those who respected Yahweh and honoured his¦381054 name¦381058.
\v 17 “They'll be¦381060 mine,” says¦381062 army-commander¦381064 Yahweh¦381063. “On¦381071 the day¦381065 when¦381066 I \add ≈assemble\add* my treasured possession¦381069, I \add ≈won't punish\add* \add @those¦381071 people\add*, just¦381072 like a \add ≈father doesn't punish\add* his¦381077 son¦381077 who¦381078 \add ≈obeys\add* him¦381079.
\v 18 Then¦381081 once again¦381081 you'll all \add ≈be able to see¦381082 the difference\add* between righteous¦381084 \add >people\add* and wicked¦381085 \add >people\add*—between \add #those\add* who serve¦381091 God¦381088 and \add #those\add* who don't¦381090.
\c 4
\s1 Be ready for future judgement
\rem /s1 The Day of the Lord; The Coming Day of Judgment; The Day of the Lord Is Coming; The Great Day of the Lord
\p
\v 1 “\add ≈Yes,\add* listen, the day that burns like a furnace is coming, when all the arrogant \add >people\add* and all the evildoers will become \add ≈useless pieces of dry stalks in a field\add*. The day that is coming will burn them up,” says army-commander Yahweh, “so \add ≈they'll be gone without leaving any\add* roots or branches.
\v 2 But for you who respect my name, the sun of righteousness will rise \add ≈and bring\add* healing. You'll all go out, jumping around like calves \add let out of their\add* stall,
\v 3 and you'll all trample down the wicked \add >people\add*, because they'll \add just\add* be ashes under the soles of your feet on the day that I act,” says army-commander Yahweh.
\p
\v 4 “\add ≈Be sure to obey\add* the law that I \add ≈gave\add* my servant Mosheh at \add ≈Mt. Sinai\add* for all Israel—the statutes and the rulings.
\p
\v 5 Listen, I'll send the prophet Eliyah to you all, \add ahead\add* of the coming of the great \add ≈but\add* fearful day of \add *my\add* \add judgement\add*.\x + \xo 4:5: \xt Mat 11:14; 17:10-13; Mrk 9:11-13; Luk 1:17; Yhn 1:21.\x*
\v 6 He'll \add ≈restore harmony between fathers and their children\add*, so that I don't \add have to\add* come and strike the earth with complete destruction.”
